bitrary constant.\n\nWe start by factoring the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dP}{dt} & =0.05P-0.000\\,5{P}^{2} \\\\  & =0.000\\,5P(100-P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,5,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=100.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-(100\\cdot 0.000\\,5)t}}=\\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-0.05t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=5$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{100}{1+C{e}^{-0.05(0)}} & =5 \\\\ 1+C & =20 \\\\ C & =19\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{100}{1+19{e}^{-0.05t}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=11$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(11) & =\\frac{100}{1+19{e}^{-0.05(11)}} \\\\  & ≈8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $11$ years, approximately $8$ turtles inhabited the island." 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327382 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327383 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327384 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327385 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327386 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1041 "selection" 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327384 13194139535023 true] [17592186327381 1110 #uuid "ccdf6183-a13b-5676-b67b-e64e469c9685" 13194139535023 true] [17592186327382 1034 "12" 13194139535023 true] [17592186327382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535023 true] [17592186327382 1111 #uuid "f2270adc-ac34-5a91-96c4-38b5616bdc6d" 13194139535023 true] [17592186327383 1034 "19" 13194139535023 true] [17592186327383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535023 true] [17592186327383 1111 #uuid "1f4192d8-01d9-5fee-a36b-a00545f09a48" 13194139535023 true] [17592186327384 1034 "8" 131941395